  "details": "As mentioned in title, currently if you have a large group that has a lot of banned users >7601 you will not be able to go through and list all of the banned users. This \n\n1. Prevents you unbanning users through the website without a use of 3rd party tools\n\n2. It prevents you from checking and listing old banned users\n\nI believe it must either \n\n1. Be increased same as the Get Members \"/members\" endpoint got increased which is now at 100K, obvious problem with bans is the banned member count could be \"theoretically\" infinite.\n\n2. Some sort of filtering must be implemented eg. ideal filtering option would be filtering by \"bannedAt\" which will allow time-based searches",
